      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 30% increase in mean values of net weight of the heart and the weight of its individual portions in 88 males, who had suffered from coronary disease and died suddenly as a result of the first major coronary disaster (in the absence of postinfarction scars and systemic arterial hypertension) was indicative of an evenly distributed compensatory myocardial hypertrophy of the entire heart. Therefore, detection of increased heart weight may be used as an additional indicator for intravital and postmortem diagnosis of early and latent coronary heart disease."},
